Reference software used as VERIFICATION ORACLES, never vendored or linked:
ffmpeg (LGPL/GPL) for H.264 pixel references, header traces and ATRAC3plus
decoding; the ITU-T H.264 JM reference software (its own licence) for
syntax-element traces. No code from either is reproduced here.

One exception, the ATRAC3plus TABLES. ATRAC3plus has no public specification;
its Huffman codebooks, weight and shape tables, quantiser steps, noise table and
IPQF prototype filter are known only as the data of ffmpeg's reverse-engineered
decoder (libavcodec/atrac3plus_data.h and atrac3plusdsp.c, (c) 2010-2013 Maxim
Poliakovski, LGPL-2.1-or-later). They are transcribed, from ffmpeg n9.0.1, by
tools/gen_at3p_tables.py into tools/at3p_tables.py and the ROM images derived
from it, and are carried under GPL-3.0-or-later as section 3 of the LGPL-2.1
permits. The decoding logic (tools/at3p_*.py, umd/at3p/) is this project's own,
written from reading ffmpeg and checked against its output.

